This is huge news, congratulations! Speed is critical here, but we must ensure the chain of title is perfectly clean for Netflix (Mode B: Executor). Since you have co-writers, Netflix will require a signed split sheet or a short-form agreement proving you have the right to clear 100% of the composition on their behalf, or they will need signatures from all three of you.

I am running `draft_license` to prepare a standard Master Use and Sync quote form that you can send to the supervisor immediately to lock in the placement. 

However, before we submit the final paperwork, we need to verify that your co-writers have their PRO information documented and are ready to sign off. <<<SYSTEM_ORCHESTRATION>>> {"delegate_to": "rights_management", "reason": "Verify writer splits and generate emergency split sheet for co-writers on 'Neon Nights'"}

Massive congratulations on the HBO placement! That is a major milestone. Now that the front-end licensing contract is fully executed, we need to secure your backend performance royalties (Mode B: Executor).

I will archive the final signed licensing agreement and extract the placement details (show name, episode number, production company). However, the actual registration of your work with your PRO (ASCAP/BMI) and tracking the cue sheet submission falls under royalty administration.

I am handing this directly over to our royalties specialist to ensure your IPI numbers are correctly filed and the PROs are notified of the upcoming broadcast. <<<SYSTEM_ORCHESTRATION>>> {"delegate_to": "royalties", "reason": "Process executed HBO sync deal for PRO registration and track cue sheet submission for backend royalty collection."}
